From: EglantinePS5 <Vampinity@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: up: ASTC scan chunks, the ASTC opacity scan reads 16 KiB at a time (EDEN_UP_ASTC_SCAN_CHUNKS)

Port of waveydude/Eglantine-PS5- e86889c515f5ecac1fde6519c62c6335e39ef8c4 (his core patch 0917,
"Scan ASTC opacity with fixed-size scratch"), credit waveydude; the chunked loop is his, line for
line (only the buffer name differs: astc_scan_chunk, a new member, because the old vector stays for
the off path and for verify).

What: JoinImages decides whether a new ASTC image is opaque (then it is re-packed as BC1, half the
size of BC3) by reading the whole image into the growing astc_scan_buffer. His crash 20261111-095523
was that resize: operator new refused 32,435,200 bytes on the GPU back thread with 4 MiB free.
EDEN_UP_HEAP_HOLDERS (0535) frees the buffer only after a scan over 8 MiB; it does not stop the growth.

Switch EDEN_UP_ASTC_SCAN_CHUNKS (boot, read once; exact 1 or 2, anything else off; off by default):
  1  read and check the image 16 KiB at a time through a fixed array in the cache object, stopping
     at the first block with alpha. IsOpaque judges each 16-byte block on its own and 16 KiB is a
     whole number of blocks, so the answer is the same and no heap is asked for at scan time.
  2  verify: the chunked scan, then the old whole-image scan, whose answer is used; differences are
     counted (expect 0). Keeps the old resize (the old risk): a check arm, not a crash arm. Do not
     pair it with EDEN_UP_NEW_WAIT_MS (a refused resize would then wait under the texture-cache lock).
  Both print "EDEN_UP_ASTC_SCAN_CHUNKS 10s:" (scans, MiB read, MiB skipped by the early stop, scans
  over 8 MiB, largest KiB, verified, differ), on the GPU back thread, at most every 10 s, only after
  a scan.

Cost when off: a few tests of one static int per ASTC join, then the old lines unchanged
(re-indented into an else). The cache object grows by 16 KiB plus 64 bytes of counters, once, at
boot. No waits, no locks, no picture change.

Review corrections applied (review of the draft): the switch text is read with value[0] tested
before value[1] (an empty value read one byte past the end); the comment and this header say "a few
tests of one static int".
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
index ed8ef94..409389d 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
@@ -5683,14 +5683,83 @@ ImageId TextureCache<P>::JoinImages(const ImageInfo& info, GPUVAddr gpu_addr, DA
         if (IsPixelFormatASTC(new_info.format) && runtime.UseOpaqueAstcFormat()) {
             const size_t scan_bytes = CalculateGuestSizeInBytes(new_info);
             if (scan_bytes <= MaxScanBytes) {
-                astc_scan_buffer.resize(scan_bytes);
-                gpu_memory->ReadBlockUnsafe(gpu_addr, astc_scan_buffer.data(), scan_bytes);
-                new_info.astc_opaque = AstcDataLooksOpaque(astc_scan_buffer);
-                static const bool trim = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_HEAP_HOLDERS");
-                if (trim && astc_scan_buffer.capacity() > (size_t{8} << 20)) {
-                    std::vector<u8>{}.swap(astc_scan_buffer);
+                // EDEN_UP_ASTC_SCAN_CHUNKS (waveydude e86889c, his 0917): 1 reads and checks the
+                // image 16 KiB at a time through the fixed astc_scan_chunk and stops at the first
+                // block with alpha, so the scan never grows a heap scratch to the texture's size
+                // (his GPUBack crash: a refused 32,435,200-byte resize with 4 MiB free). ASTC
+                // blocks are 16 bytes and IsOpaque judges each on its own, and 16 KiB is a whole
+                // number of blocks, so the answer is the same. 2 = verify: the chunked scan runs,
+                // then the old whole-image scan, whose answer is used; differences are counted.
+                // Unset: a few tests of one static int, then the old path below, unchanged.
+                static const int scan_chunks = [] {
+                    const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_UP_ASTC_SCAN_CHUNKS");
+                    if (value == nullptr || value[0] == '\0' || value[1] != '\0') {
+                        return 0;
+                    }
+                    return value[0] == '1' ? 1 : value[0] == '2' ? 2 : 0;
+                }();
+                bool chunked_opaque = true;
+                if (scan_chunks != 0) {
+                    size_t scanned = 0;
+                    for (size_t offset = 0; offset < scan_bytes; offset += astc_scan_chunk.size()) {
+                        const size_t bytes = (std::min)(scan_bytes - offset, astc_scan_chunk.size());
+                        const auto chunk = std::span{astc_scan_chunk}.first(bytes);
+                        gpu_memory->ReadBlockUnsafe(gpu_addr + offset, chunk.data(), chunk.size());
+                        scanned += bytes;
+                        if (!AstcDataLooksOpaque(chunk)) {
+                            chunked_opaque = false;
+                            break;
+                        }
+                    }
+                    ++astc_chunk_scans;
+                    astc_chunk_read_bytes += scanned;
+                    astc_chunk_skipped_bytes += scan_bytes - scanned;
+                    astc_chunk_largest = (std::max)(astc_chunk_largest, static_cast<u64>(scan_bytes));
+                    if (scan_bytes > (size_t{8} << 20)) {
+                        ++astc_chunk_big_scans;
+                    }
+                }
+                if (scan_chunks == 1) {
+                    new_info.astc_opaque = chunked_opaque;
+                } else {
+                    astc_scan_buffer.resize(scan_bytes);
+                    gpu_memory->ReadBlockUnsafe(gpu_addr, astc_scan_buffer.data(), scan_bytes);
+                    new_info.astc_opaque = AstcDataLooksOpaque(astc_scan_buffer);
+                    static const bool trim = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_HEAP_HOLDERS");
+                    if (trim && astc_scan_buffer.capacity() > (size_t{8} << 20)) {
+                        std::vector<u8>{}.swap(astc_scan_buffer);
+                    }
+                    if (scan_chunks == 2) {
+                        ++astc_chunk_verified;
+                        if (chunked_opaque != new_info.astc_opaque) {
+                            ++astc_chunk_differ;
+                        }
+                    }
                 }
                 ++(new_info.astc_opaque ? astc_opaque_images : astc_alpha_images);
+                if (scan_chunks != 0) {
+                    const auto now = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
+                    if (astc_chunk_last_log == std::chrono::steady_clock::time_point{}) {
+                        astc_chunk_last_log = now;
+                    } else if (now - astc_chunk_last_log >= std::chrono::seconds(10)) {
+                        std::fprintf(
+                            stderr,
+                            "EDEN_UP_ASTC_SCAN_CHUNKS 10s: mode %d, scans %llu, read %llu MiB, "
+                            "skipped by early stop %llu MiB, scans over 8 MiB %llu, largest %llu "
+                            "KiB, verified %llu, differ %llu\n",
+                            scan_chunks, static_cast<unsigned long long>(astc_chunk_scans),
+                            static_cast<unsigned long long>(astc_chunk_read_bytes >> 20),
+                            static_cast<unsigned long long>(astc_chunk_skipped_bytes >> 20),
+                            static_cast<unsigned long long>(astc_chunk_big_scans),
+                            static_cast<unsigned long long>(astc_chunk_largest >> 10),
+                            static_cast<unsigned long long>(astc_chunk_verified),
+                            static_cast<unsigned long long>(astc_chunk_differ));
+                        astc_chunk_last_log = now;
+                        astc_chunk_scans = astc_chunk_read_bytes = astc_chunk_skipped_bytes = 0;
+                        astc_chunk_big_scans = astc_chunk_largest = 0;
+                        astc_chunk_verified = astc_chunk_differ = 0;
+                    }
+                }
             }
         }
     }
diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h
index 3de1a4d..fab3ace 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h
